      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is very nearly there, but the management of the lock needs a little more refinement.  Right now, it is held unnecessarily during error handling in the callback and during _success_ handling in the processing, even though the synchronization is only needed across 2 or 3 lines of code in both places.  That widens the window of opportunity for lock contention in both places, increasing the likelihood of dropping reasons.\n\nThe RAII approach to locks in C++ is very powerful, but just because we _can_ let locks be auto-released when they naturally go out of scope doesn\u0027t mean we _should_ let it happen (vs. either manual unlocking or structurally forcing them to go out of scope as soon as they\u0027re no longer needed).",
      "revId": "42ac3858efffc9b1f11881955847ca4279d9e5c6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
