      "writtenOn": "2020-10-27T05:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the reasons I structured this a bit differently in my suggestion (if I\u0027m remembering correctly) is that when the code is structured this way, if you get the lock on line 124 and find that mWakeupReasons is not empty, the lock remains held for all of this logging activity, which unnecessarily widens the window for potential lock contention.  There\u0027s nothing wrong with the way the logic is constructed in terms of correctness, but it\u0027s almost always better to give up locks before doing error logging unless the locks actually protect something related to the logging.",
      "revId": "42ac3858efffc9b1f11881955847ca4279d9e5c6",
